untime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BeKmQoX9z7y4CMu6u4Vgtm", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 385247, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BeKmQoX9z7y4CMu6u4Vgtm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 389560, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), which the test expects. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory system didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against it. The fix is based on the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR because that needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013EvE6z7ttM4ZseXvKP4puq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XqqgsThNUKjT4A4BtkBDxs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CZJ7xvwvGC9D3TKovgXhyD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01H5qNuCrCXaXzU5RLYkFMr7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012SXbefzxK2QHTYUvtWCBKB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01C8eADd9pxJa6cKWWbmTpjc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GzdvWjWD6mTtzRkyxdBMrN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BeKmQoX9z7y4CMu6u4Vgtm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN)", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring says otherwise.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 \u2014 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), which the test expects. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory system didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against it. The fix is based on the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR because that needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}